Rotator cuff pain, tendinopathy, and tears (@shoulder-cuff-problems: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @shoulder, #source @med-source-cuff-patient, #source @med-source-tendinopathy-guideline, #source @med-source-cuff-guideline, #medicine @shoulder-calcific, #orthopedics @shoulder-calcific, #shoulder @shoulder-calcific) { r_16SYXGMD8KFKTSXAC8G1HHH4EW
**Read selected problem descriptions:** [Rotator cuff tears — AAOS](../../../sources/Rotator-cuff-tears-AAOS.lingua#r_5G6SQ0913D89PSPG03A3XYDQ5W), the anatomy, tear descriptions, Symptoms, and Doctor’s Examination sections. Then read only the scope and definitions of [Rotator Cuff Tendinopathy — JOSPT, 2025](../../../sources/Tendinopathy-guideline-2025.lingua#r_74MJTFK7YKMV06M2GFT8YZ5DFV) and [Management of Rotator Cuff Injuries — AAOS, 2025](../../../sources/Rotator-cuff-guideline-2025.lingua#r_5JCRVDCV75VA441X5FG5S226G3) to identify their different populations. Their full management and evidence sections belong to the later guideline study.

Rotator cuff-related pain describes a clinical problem around the cuff and related region. Tendinopathy/tendinopatia, a partial-thickness tear/ruptura parcial, and a full-thickness tear/ruptura transfixante describe different concepts and findings. A full-thickness tear does not necessarily mean that the tendon has separated across its entire width.

A tear can occur in a traumatic or longer-developing context. Some tears are painless; symptom severity and structural extent cannot be treated as the same measurement. The history, examination, function, and imaging question help determine relevance.

'Impingement' or 'síndrome do impacto' appears in older and current sources with varying meanings. A purely mechanical pinching story should not be assumed to explain every cuff-related complaint or to establish that removing bone will help. The later trial reading examines this reasoning directly.

**Try:** compare a fictional partial-tear report with a fictional full-thickness report. List what each establishes anatomically and what remains unknown about pain, function, progression, and treatment benefit.

**Continue:** [Calcific tendinopathy — a finding and its clinical context](Calcific-tendinopathy.lingua#r_2KW7TDWEPVWRJ8NE03W636FW51).

